+// Patched (pnpm patch, see docs/patches.md): emphasis that cannot close is
+// turned away before emStrong walks the rest of the paragraph for its closer.
+//
+// The walk takes each run of * or _ that could open and looks for the run that
+// closes it, so a paragraph of openers nothing closes is quadratic: `*a ` a
+// hundred thousand characters long took 162 seconds. The walk is a running
+// count over the runs of emStrongRDelimAst and emStrongRDelimUnd: it starts at
+// the opener's length, a run that can only open adds its length, one that can
+// close takes it away, one that can do both takes it away unless the rule of
+// three makes it neither, and the opener closes once the count is down to
+// nothing. What a run counts as depends only on the characters either side of
+// it, so the counts are summed once per paragraph, and a running minimum from
+// the end says whether an opener's count ever gets there. If it cannot, the
+// walk would find nothing and is skipped. Emphasis nested thousands deep ran
+// out of stack, so it is read EM_DEEPEST deep and no further. Read off the GFM
+// rules (marked's default); pedantic and non-GFM reading is left as it was.
